        "id": 191555,
        "name": "bolnerap",
        "username": "bolnerap",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bolnerap/{size}/6056_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-03-08T03:36:20.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Mint. Took a little over an hour. &nbsp;I probably went overboard with prep, but taking care of her post-flip was pretty easy.</p><p>I had a long chat with a coworker today about this match, and we concluded that I should try it like Skinwalker Gloomweaver; get as set up as possible, and go nuts after the flip. So, that's what I did. &nbsp;Parse was easily the MVP of the match. &nbsp;Here's roughly how it went down, keeping in mind that this was a really long match and I can't remember all the details.</p><p>Dreamer's Front Side: I got out as many ongoings as possible, some worthwhile (Aura of Vision, Hippocratic Oath, Imbued Fire, Extrasensory Awareness, 3x Crit Multiplier, 2x Exploit Vulnerability, all the Bounties) and some destruction fodder (Flesh of the Sun God, Living Conflagration, Gauge, Drawn to the Flame). Once I found it in Parse's deck, I used Extrasensory Awareness every round to sift through Dreamer's deck and discard the really nasty stuff. I intentionally flipped her when she was down to 7 cards in her deck, all of which were Projections, all of which were Not Dark Heroes.</p><p>During this ridiculously long setup, The Sentinels ended up drawing basically their entire deck and by the end of it, they were playing Restorative Burst, using Dr. Medico's power, and using Hippocratic Oath for a total of 2 AOE healing per round. Chrono-Ranger was also healing via his healing bounty. Ra unfortunately blew up three of his staves early on to help burn through Projections, so he was relying on the Sentinels for healing. Probably could have done that better. &nbsp;Chrono-Ranger was also pinging environment targets with the NeuroToxin dart thrower in order to nullify their AOE damage, and he had The Ultimate Target on a Battalion Brute so he could get multiple Dart Thrower uses each round to help nerf the environment.</p><p>When I finally flipped the Dreamer (with all my heroes in the mid-teens for HP) by taking out that last Granite Oni, plowing through her Projections was trivial. Parse was playing Recompile every round for 9 stored damage boosts, Chrono-Ranger could do 5-6 irreducible with Masada, and 2x Exploit Vulnerability meant that any damage reduction on the board was nullified. For two rounds, Dreamer played 3 projections, the Sentinels and Chrono-Ranger absolutely obliterated them, Ra twiddled his thumbs, and Parse played another Recompile to get everyone charged up for the next round.&nbsp;</p><p>On the last round, Dreamer shuffled trash into deck and did get off a lightly boosted AOE attack, but Writhe was the only character who ended up getting incapped. Final HP 3/0/5/3, 3, 3, 9. I probably could have done a little better - charging up Hippocratic Oath instead of Mainstay / Idealist could have been healing me for 8-10 per round, and that way Ra could have actually contributed some damage. But hey, it worked out.&nbsp;</p>",
