      {
        "id": 191556,
        "name": "robb8888",
        "username": "robb8888",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-03-08T05:18:45.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"bolnerap\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bolnerap/48/6056_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> bolnerap:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Mint. Took a little over an hour. &nbsp;I probably went overboard with prep, but taking care of her post-flip was pretty easy…When I finally flipped the Dreamer (with all my heroes in the mid-teens for HP) by taking out that last Granite Oni…</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>(1) &nbsp;How did you stay alive long enough to get out all of that setup? &nbsp;Even if you take out the \"nastiest\" stuff from Dreamer's deck, it's still pretty consistent round-to-round damage, and (at least in the games I've played) the really good stuff in Chrono and Ra's deck (i.e., Imbued Fire, Blazing Tornado) that will allow you to start taking apart projections doesn't come until Round 4-5 or so. &nbsp;In my best games, by the time I have out about 8 Ongoings (i.e., enough to withstand the 4-ongoing killfest when Dreamer flips), all of my heroes are down to about 12 HP. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>(2) For that matter, when did you come across Extrasensory Awareness? &nbsp;I've been trying to play Recompile early to get cards in Parse's hand, but in all of my games (about 10 so far) I have yet to come across Extrasensory Awareness. &nbsp;I've gotten two Gauges several times, but never saw Extrasensory Awareness. &nbsp;Did you play lots of Recompiles?</p>",
