      {
        "id": 191557,
        "name": "bolnerap",
        "username": "bolnerap",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bolnerap/{size}/6056_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-03-08T08:02:14.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"robb8888\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> robb8888:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>bolnerap wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Mint. Took a little over an hour. &nbsp;I probably went overboard with prep, but taking care of her post-flip was pretty easy....When I finally flipped the Dreamer (with all my heroes in the mid-teens for HP) by taking out that last Granite Oni...\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\n(1) &nbsp;How did you stay alive long enough to get out all of that setup? ... the really good stuff in Chrono and Ra's deck (i.e., Imbued Fire, Blazing Tornado) doesn't come until Round 4-5 or so... &nbsp;In my best games, by the time I have out about 8 Ongoings (i.e., enough to withstand the 4-ongoing killfest when Dreamer flips), all of my heroes are down to about 12 HP. &nbsp;(2) For that matter, when did you come across Extrasensory Awareness? &nbsp;I've been trying to play Recompile early to get cards in Parse's hand, but in all of my games (about 10 so far) I have yet to come across Extrasensory Awareness. &nbsp;I've gotten two Gauges several times, but never saw Extrasensory Awareness. &nbsp;Did you play lots of Recompiles?\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<ol>\n<li>Likely got different shuffles. I Displaced Armoried into Neuro-Toxin Dart Thrower on turn 1 and started using it immediately to ping the initial Arachnoids. After that I searched for Masadah and started throwing out bounties, primarily on nigh-invincible Environment targets. Though I did use Kill On Sight multiple times to draw more cards (since I kept getting Ranger's Mark to easily pull KOS back out). With Ra, you get a couple Staves early and I blew them up right away to help rip up the first set of projections. I used Summon Staff to search for the last one. &nbsp;Indeed, I didn't see Imbued Fire for a long time, but as it turns out, I probably didn't need it.&nbsp;</li>\n</ol>\n<p>I also ended up with everyone in the low double digits before I got my healing loop going, but I was able to edge higher on HP before the flip with deck control and two Dart Thrower shots per round.</p>\n<ol start=\"2\">\n<li>Basically, I used every opportunity to get Parse more cards. Impossible Shot, a fairly early use of Gauge, Recompile. I was going for so much setup that I did have one relatively early Recompile where I just dumped all my copies of Reveal the Flaws because I knew I wouldn't need them. I also at one point used Syntactic Analysis on Parse, which chained into another Syntactic Analysis, letting her get several Ongoings out at once. I forget how late that was though. By the time I flipped Dreamer, I had two Extrasensory Awarenesses in play, and two of my destructions were the extra EA and Gauge (since I knew I wasn't using Gauge as long as EA was out.)</li>\n</ol>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
